# Migration assessment: `OVHcloud`

- Inventory file: `inventory.json`
- Source: `aws`
- Catalog: `OVHcloud` snapshot from `https://www.ovhcloud.com/en/public-cloud/prices/`, retrieved 2026-11-08

## Summary

| Fit | Resources |
|---|---|
| direct | 2 |
| partial | 1 |
| none | 0 |
| total | 3 |

## Resources

| ID | Raw type | Category | Fit | Best offering | Reasons |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `zone-dnssec` | `AWS::Route53::HostedZone` | `network.dns` | direct | `Apex DNS Zone` (tie: `DNS Zone` (global), `DNS Zone Premium` (global)) | `Apex DNS Zone` offers every capability the resource uses |
| `zone-example` | `AWS::Route53::HostedZone` | `network.dns` | direct | `DNS Zone` (global) (tie: `DNS Zone Premium` (global)) | `DNS Zone` offers every capability the resource uses |
| `zone-ipv6` | `AWS::Route53::HostedZone` | `network.dns` | partial | `DNS Zone` (global) (tie: `DNS Zone Premium` (global)) | `DNS Zone` does not offer `ipv6` |

`(global)` means not bound to a region you choose, including the one `--region` names: the provider serves the offering from its own locations, which may be outside the EU and which the target's `SOURCES.md` names.

## Required changes

- `zone-ipv6`: `ipv6` (not offered by `DNS Zone` (global))

## Blockers

None.
